// fixture-418: A4 (resolver-semantics RFC §3 Axis A (c)) — the ordering
// hazard the last-scheduling decision-priority rule exists for.
//
// bearssl is a version-unknown git dep (untagged branch pin, no .nimble
// version) declared BEFORE its constrainer. The constrainer, chronos, is a
// NAMED (index) dep whose own floor ("bearssl >= 0.2.8") only materializes
// LAZILY, mid-solve, the first time PubGrub selects a candidate for it — it
// is not knowable at bearssl's naive declaration-order turn.
//
// Without A4's decision-priority rule (version-unknown packages scheduled
// strictly last), bearssl would be decided at the sentinel BEFORE chronos is
// ever expanded; chronos's later-discovered floor would then conflict with
// the already-decided bearssl and degrade to a generic SOLVE-CONFLICT after
// backtracking exhausts both single-candidate packages — never this
// fixture's crisp RES-VERSION-UNKNOWN-CONSTRAINED. With A4, chronos (not
// version-unknown) is decided first, its floor lands in bearssl's
// accumulated range, and only THEN is bearssl classified — at a decision
// point where the range is guaranteed complete.
name "myapp"
kind "application"
deps {
    bearssl git=(url)"https://example.com/bearssl.git" ref="main"
    chronos
}
